course: dictionary
lesson: 15187
title: Words of direction
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Seawards» tells you which way something is moving. It means towards the sea, away from the land. Break it into two parts: sea, and wards, which means in the direction of.
explain: «The tide flowed seawards, leaving rock pools behind.» The rock pools are left on the beach, so the water must have moved away from the shore. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The tide flowed towards the sea, leaving rock pools behind" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: «Seawards» is a direction word, like «homewards» and «skywards». In each one, the ending «-wards» shows the way something moves: towards home, towards the sky, towards the sea.
fact: Seawards means towards the sea, away from the land.
fact: «Seawards» is an adverb. «Seaward» can be an adjective or an adverb.
fact: «The boat sailed seawards as the sun went down.» Sailors use this word to describe a ship's direction.
fact: Beach safety signs warn that a rip current can carry swimmers seawards, so swimmers should not fight against it.
fact: Other direction words: «homewards» means towards home, and «skywards» means towards the sky.
exercise: «The tide flowed seawards, leaving rock pools behind.» What does seawards mean? | Up into the sky | Towards the land, away from the sea | Along the beach, to the left | *Towards the sea, away from the land
exercise: «The boat sailed seawards as the sun went down.» Find and copy the word that gives the direction. | down | *seawards | sun | boat
exercise: «The wind blew the kite seawards.» Which way did the kite go? | Back onto the beach | Round in a circle | *Out to sea, away from the land | Straight down into the sand
test: «The swimmers were told not to drift seawards.» What does drift seawards mean? | Walk slowly up the beach | *Float slowly towards the sea | Dive under the waves | Lie still on the sand
test: «The sailors faced seawards as the ship left the harbour.» Which way did they face? | *Towards the sea | Towards the town | Towards the sky | Towards the back of the ship
exam: «Ella stood on the pier and watched the boat head seawards.» Where was the boat going? | Up into the hills | *Out towards the sea, away from the land | Back to the harbour | Round and round the bay
